<!-- template name="page-hero" {"kicker":"About Popular Retro","title":"We're old school.","lede":"The modern world is a lovely place, loads of gadgets, toys, expensive shiny things and all of that jazz (if you're into that kinda thing). Here at Popular Retro, we're old school.","image":"https://greemo-popularretro.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/media/images/boombox.jpg","imageAlt":"An old boombox in a derelict room","stripe":true} -->

<!-- template name="story-split" {"kicker":"By enthusiasts, for enthusiasts","title":"Fresh content, sliced from an old cake","body":"Popular Retro is a magazine for retro enthusiasts, written by retro enthusiasts. We've a combined age* that could be likened to a fine wine or a dusty old chair that lurks in the darkest corner of an old country house.\\n\\nYou can be assured of fresh content but sliced from a cake baked many years ago (it's still tasty).\\n\\nEach issue we'll be looking back at classic games, toys, movies, music and culture. Join us on our journey, we've plenty of memories to share with you!","note":"* We're old, but still have some life left in us!","topicsTitle":"What we cover","topics":["Classic gaming","Home computers","Toys","Movies and B-movies","TV","Music","Comics","Fashion and culture","Obscure media formats"],"asideTitle":"The journey so far","asideBody":"Five free digital issues from Winter 2018 to October 2020, a collector's hardback in February 2021, and the first print issue in June 2021."} -->

<!-- template name="team-grid" {"kicker":"The team","title":"Who makes it","text":"Contributors to Volume 2, Issue 1.","gap":"Current team, bios and photos from Jan","people":[{"name":"Darren Randle","role":"Editor"},{"name":"Darren Branagh","role":"Contributor"},{"name":"Shaun Bebbington","role":"Contributor"},{"name":"Luis Mota","role":"Contributor"},{"name":"Chris Thacker","role":"Contributor"},{"name":"Dr. Chris","role":"Contributor"}]} -->

